WEBVTT

00:35.582 --> 00:38.043
<i>We now return to
The Adventures of Aquaman.</i>

00:45.717 --> 00:48.469
- Yeah?
- Hey, can you grab me another beer?

00:48.804 --> 00:51.473
<i>Yeah. Anything else?
Maybe, you know, TV Guide,</i>

00:51.598 --> 00:53.558
you know, another pillow for your feet
or something?

00:53.642 --> 00:57.605
No. Actually, you know what?
Get me, like, a Dewar's and soda, and,

00:57.938 --> 01:00.399
you know, try to keep the saltwater
out of it, if you could.

01:00.483 --> 01:02.609
- Try to keep the saltwater...
- Yeah.

01:02.692 --> 01:05.445
We're surrounded by saltwater, you know.
It's kind of difficult.

01:05.569 --> 01:07.614
I know. I'm just saying,
I'm just saying, try.

01:07.739 --> 01:08.741
Yeah, okay, I'll try.

01:08.825 --> 01:11.034
- You want me to wipe your ass, too?
- Oh, that's a helpful tone.

01:11.160 --> 01:14.412
I'm just saying, you're kind of abusing
your powers a little bit, don't you think?

01:14.496 --> 01:17.082
Actually, this is all time that
could be spent getting me my beverage.

01:17.164 --> 01:18.291
Hey, what are you guys doing?

01:18.375 --> 01:20.836
We got to get ready for your grandpa's
80th birthday dinner.

01:20.961 --> 01:23.629
- Peter, calm down. He's just your father.
- Yeah, but I love him.

01:23.754 --> 01:27.300
His folksy racism,
his I-don't-care-where-I-am flatulence.

01:27.425 --> 01:29.052
And the way it always seems like
he's chewing,

01:29.178 --> 01:30.637
even when there's no food in there.

01:32.847 --> 01:36.309
- Hiya, Dad.
- Francis, it's so good to see you.

01:36.518 --> 01:39.645
Lois, you haven't changed a bit,
you lying bitch.

01:40.688 --> 01:43.065
Francis, why don't you come
into the dining room, huh?

01:43.191 --> 01:45.319
The table's all set for your birthday dinner.

01:45.484 --> 01:49.864
Lois, actually, Dad said
he would prefer it if you did not join us,

01:50.032 --> 01:52.742
you know, you being a Protestant and all.

01:52.867 --> 01:54.661
He said it's okay if you sit
at the kid's table.

01:54.786 --> 01:56.496
Peter, I cooked the damn dinner.

01:56.579 --> 01:59.666
You know, I knew you were going to
react like this, and that's why

01:59.791 --> 02:01.835
I brought Bill Lumbergh
to explain it to you.

02:01.918 --> 02:06.547
Yeah, I'm going to need you to go ahead
and not complain about this.

02:06.673 --> 02:10.552
Oh, and if you could go ahead
and sit at the kids' table,

02:10.677 --> 02:12.137
that'd be great.

02:14.096 --> 02:17.600
I'm just saying, '70s boobs were different.
I don't know.

02:17.767 --> 02:20.353
You know, it wouldn't kill you
to contribute to the conversation.

02:20.520 --> 02:24.815
Dad, tell us about World War I and how
America defeated Kaiser Permanente.

02:24.899 --> 02:27.693
Lois, when are you going to
get that baby baptized?

02:27.777 --> 02:29.487
Oh, God, not this again.

02:29.571 --> 02:32.072
Francis, why the hell is this always
an issue with you?

02:32.198 --> 02:36.702
Because I love this family and
I don't want my grandson to burn in hell.

02:36.827 --> 02:41.749
I love you, Grandpa. Your toenails
are the same color as my school bus.

02:42.042 --> 02:44.961
You really think that
splashing magic water on Stewie

02:45.086 --> 02:46.128
will keep him out of hell?

02:46.254 --> 02:49.090
Watch that kind of talk
or you'll get your heathen head smacked.

02:49.215 --> 02:50.215
Oh, that's very Christian.

02:50.341 --> 02:52.551
- "Believe what I say or I'll hurt you. "
- Now you're getting it.

02:56.597 --> 02:57.724
Peter, we have a problem.

02:57.849 --> 02:59.475
Hey, hang on, Lois. I'm watching a movie.

02:59.601 --> 03:02.353
<i>And now back to Jaws V,
Fire Island.</i>

03:02.728 --> 03:07.191
<i>- You think we should be this far out?
- Stop worrying, Mark. We'll be fine.</i>

03:07.442 --> 03:11.404
<i>Hey, I'm gonna eat you all.
I'm gonna eat that hairy leg.</i>

03:12.322 --> 03:16.284
<i>I'm gonna eat that one, too.
Oh, I can see right up them shorts.</i>

03:16.951 --> 03:20.371
<i>I got a whole bunch of rows of teeth
to chew you with.</i>

03:22.456 --> 03:26.752
<i>Oh, now wait a minute. I did have
a chubby kid on a raft earlier today.</i>

03:26.919 --> 03:30.089
<i>It's okay, though.
I've been swimming a lot lately.</i>

03:30.214 --> 03:31.339
<i>Yummy.</i>

03:31.966 --> 03:34.885
Peter, your father won't let up
about Stewie getting baptized.

03:34.968 --> 03:38.431
I am sick of him always trying to force
his religious views on us.

03:38.598 --> 03:40.641
All right, I'll talk to him, Lois,
but, you know,

03:40.767 --> 03:43.644
when my father wants something,
it's like sex with Kobe Bryant.

03:43.769 --> 03:47.691
You can kick and scream all you want,
but it's gonna happen.

03:50.984 --> 03:53.654
- Dad, what are you doing?
- There's no cross in here.

03:53.779 --> 03:55.531
Every kitchen needs a crucifix.

03:55.655 --> 03:58.617
Oh, yes. Nothing says, "Eat up,"
like a bleeding, half-naked Jew

03:58.742 --> 03:59.785
nailed to a piece of wood.

03:59.911 --> 04:02.288
Listen, Dad, I gotta talk to you.

04:02.372 --> 04:06.917
Lois was wondering if maybe you could,
I don't know, ease up on the whole,

04:07.459 --> 04:10.880
you know, Jesus-ay Christ-ay,
if you catch my drift.

04:11.005 --> 04:12.798
You're a lapsed Catholic, Peter.

04:12.882 --> 04:16.385
Your wife's a Protestant whore
and your baby isn't even baptized.

04:16.510 --> 04:18.971
All right, look, Dad,
I don't want you to hate me, all right?

04:19.054 --> 04:20.348
So I'll make a deal with you.

04:20.472 --> 04:24.477
If we get Stewie baptized, you and
all other old people have to acknowledge

04:24.560 --> 04:27.605
and be aware that there's crap
in the corners of your mouth.

04:27.688 --> 04:29.815
I'll think about it. Now let's go.

04:29.898 --> 04:32.818
Old people are gross, no matter how cute
they try to make them look

04:32.901 --> 04:35.111
<i>on Desperate Housewives. Go ahead.</i>

04:35.195 --> 04:38.198
Switch over to ABC for five seconds.
I'll wait. I'll wait five seconds.

04:42.537 --> 04:45.998
Oh, my God, did you see?
Did you see how old and ugly they are?

04:46.081 --> 04:49.209
Oh, my God, that redhead looks like
somebody pulled Silly Putty

04:49.335 --> 04:50.293
over their knee.

04:53.046 --> 04:56.801
I'm sorry, Mr. Griffin,
but I can't baptize little Stewie today.

04:56.884 --> 04:59.511
It turns out our last shipment
of holy water is tainted.

04:59.637 --> 05:02.347
Tainted? Holy water?
How did that happen?

05:10.981 --> 05:13.692
We'll call you
when we get a new shipment in.

05:13.817 --> 05:16.529
There's no such thing
as tainted holy water.

05:16.654 --> 05:18.196
Come on. We'll do it ourselves.

05:18.280 --> 05:23.243
Stewie Griffin, I baptize you in the name
of the Father, the Son and the Holy Ghost.

05:23.327 --> 05:25.203
- And Space Ghost.
- What are you doing?

05:25.288 --> 05:28.707
Oh, my God! This is almost as bad as
my bath with Kathy Bates.

05:32.253 --> 05:34.254
Yeah, I think I'm going to get out.

05:38.508 --> 05:40.718
Stewie, you don't look so good.

05:40.844 --> 05:43.722
Oh, baby, you're burning up! Oh, my God!

05:43.805 --> 05:46.141
Stewie, Stewie, speak to me!

05:46.266 --> 05:49.894
Don't... Don't take me to a black doctor.

05:52.564 --> 05:54.357
Mr. And Mrs. Griffin,
I've examined your son

05:54.441 --> 05:56.485
and he is suffering from
a temporary toxic anemia

05:56.610 --> 05:58.570
which has substantially weakened
his immune system.

05:58.653 --> 05:59.863
Is he gonna die?

05:59.947 --> 06:02.950
No, but he's highly vulnerable to infection
and must be quarantined

06:03.075 --> 06:04.701
in a germ-free plastic environment.

06:04.785 --> 06:07.579
My God, you mean like John Travolta
in that movie?

06:07.704 --> 06:10.832
<i>Oh, no, you're gonna take his face off,
like in Face/Off?</i>

06:11.083 --> 06:13.586
Well, it looks like the operation
was a success.

06:13.711 --> 06:17.631
Do you know what the best part of this is?
Try licking yourself.

06:18.215 --> 06:19.466
You bastard!

06:19.800 --> 06:22.052
<i>Peter, he meant
The Boy in the Plastic Bubble.</i>

06:22.136 --> 06:23.387
How could this have happened?

06:23.470 --> 06:26.472
It's obvious to me that Stewie's
been exposed to tainted holy water.

06:26.555 --> 06:29.560
Peter, you had Stewie baptized
behind my back?

06:29.643 --> 06:30.686
Come on, honey.

06:30.810 --> 06:32.604
This is no worse than
when I rented out your uterus

06:32.728 --> 06:34.147
to those inner city immigrants.

06:39.652 --> 06:42.782
Peter, you're a complete slave
to your father's religion.

06:42.865 --> 06:46.826
What about your religious beliefs, huh?
You have a choice, you know.

06:46.951 --> 06:49.371
- I do?
- Of course. You're a grown man.

06:49.496 --> 06:52.332
- You can pick any religion you want.
- Really?

06:53.458 --> 06:54.960
You know, Lois, maybe you're right.

06:55.043 --> 06:58.505
Maybe I should pick my own religion.
The question is, which one?

06:58.589 --> 07:01.008
I'll tell you what you can pick.
A tune out on that piano.

07:05.428 --> 07:07.473
Oh, now how the whiz-bang
does the rest of it go?

07:07.598 --> 07:09.558
Quick! Make something up!

07:18.775 --> 07:21.444
Peter, what are all these women
doing in our living room?

07:21.528 --> 07:24.031
Lois, I took your advice
and picked a new religion.

07:24.156 --> 07:27.157
- I'm gonna be a Mormon.
- A Mormon? Are you sure?

07:27.283 --> 07:30.287
Come on. Nailing a different wife
every night? That's a no-brainer.

07:30.371 --> 07:33.665
Oh, Lois, this is Kimmy,
the checkout girl from the Korean market.

07:33.748 --> 07:36.543
Nancy, our postal carrier.
And you know Tiffany,

07:36.668 --> 07:39.504
the filthy woman who stands downtown
and screams at traffic.

07:39.630 --> 07:41.839
I ate a tube of Crest for dinner!

07:41.965 --> 07:46.010
Isn't she funny? She's definitely
the Kramer of my Mormon wives.

07:46.136 --> 07:49.806
- Nancy, get me a beer.
- Mormons aren't allowed to drink alcohol.

07:54.393 --> 07:56.479
Peter, did you just
throw those women away?

07:56.562 --> 07:57.855
No. Maybe.

08:02.069 --> 08:04.654
<i>Also in the news,
some trouble at St. Phillips Church.</i>

08:04.737 --> 08:05.864
<i>That's right, Diane.</i>

08:05.947 --> 08:09.201
<i>A shipment of tainted holy water
could put some local babies in jeopardy.</i>

08:09.284 --> 08:10.744
<i>Sounds dangerous, Tom.</i>

08:10.826 --> 08:13.037
<i>Be careful next time you're at confession
telling the priest</i>

08:13.121 --> 08:15.373
<i>about cheating on your wife
with that Filipino drag queen.</i>

08:15.456 --> 08:18.292
<i>Well, at least you're in no danger, Diane,
since you only visit church</i>

08:18.418 --> 08:21.629
<i>to leave your self-delivered, unwashed,
half-dead newborns on the back step.</i>

08:21.754 --> 08:25.341
<i>Coming up, how to turn
your unwanted change into folding money.</i>

08:25.758 --> 08:28.261
You know, it's kind of sad seeing Stewie
in that plastic bubble.

08:28.385 --> 08:32.306
- I think he looks like a bunny.
- Oh, that's it, Chris, keep laughing.

08:32.515 --> 08:34.476
When I get out of here,
you're going to get it.

08:34.601 --> 08:38.855
I'll lull you into a false sense of security
like those network television announcers.

08:38.938 --> 08:40.439
<i>Tonight
on an all-new Mama's Family,</i>

08:40.564 --> 08:43.235
<i>Mama's got more than she can handle
with the in-laws in town.</i>

08:43.318 --> 08:46.487
<i>A deadly fire
could spell death for a honeymoon couple</i>

08:46.612 --> 08:48.364
<i>on an all-new Hotel.</i>

08:48.447 --> 08:50.949
<i>Tonight on Newhart,
the stockings are stuffed with comedy</i>

08:51.033 --> 08:52.452
<i>when Bob has to play Santa Claus.</i>

08:52.535 --> 08:54.621
<i>Then, a sniper's bullet
threatens a partnership</i>

08:54.745 --> 08:56.581
<i>on an all-new Cagney and Lacey.</i>

08:56.664 --> 08:58.415
<i>Tonight on a laugh-out-loud Night Court,</i>

08:58.540 --> 09:02.086
<i>love is in the air when Judge Harry's
old high-school flame comes to town.</i>

09:02.211 --> 09:04.922
<i>Then, a child's death could mean
the case of Arnie Becker's life</i>

09:05.005 --> 09:06.466
<i>on an all-new L.A. Law.</i>

09:06.591 --> 09:07.550
<i>That's Night Court at 8:00.</i>

09:07.675 --> 09:09.010
<i>L.A. Law at 9:00.</i>

09:10.136 --> 09:11.971
Now remember, kids, don't touch Stewie.

09:12.096 --> 09:14.557
He's not allowed to have
any human contact.

09:16.809 --> 09:20.021
Hey, finish the job, idiot!
For God's sakes, there's no ventilation!

09:20.145 --> 09:22.065
It smells like Brian Dennehy in here!

09:22.148 --> 09:26.444
I see London, I see France,
I see Stewie's unsightly chapped ass.

09:26.527 --> 09:28.946
Hey, gay-bo, I'm up here. Up here.

09:31.449 --> 09:32.657
Hi, my name's Peter.

09:32.783 --> 09:34.993
I'm a Jehovah's Witness,
here to spread the good news

09:35.118 --> 09:36.662
of the story of Jesus Christ.

09:36.788 --> 09:39.332
- Okay, go ahead.
- Really?

09:39.874 --> 09:41.041
Wow.

09:41.584 --> 09:44.879
Boy, you're the first person
who didn't slam the door on me.

09:45.004 --> 09:47.798
Okay, well,

09:47.882 --> 09:50.968
Jesus was a miracle worker, of sorts.

09:51.344 --> 09:55.973
He would travel from place to place,
putting things right that once went wrong

09:56.556 --> 10:00.603
and hoping each time that his next leap
would be the leap home.

10:06.232 --> 10:08.486
What do you think you're doing
with my wife?

10:08.819 --> 10:09.779
Oh, boy.

10:15.450 --> 10:19.621
The pathway to enlightenment
starts with an unfettered, focused mind.

10:19.705 --> 10:21.874
- Look out!
- What are you doing?

10:22.000 --> 10:25.002
Oh? I thought that dot on your head
was from a sniper rifle.

10:25.084 --> 10:28.130
Peter, this spot is a sacred adornment.

10:28.213 --> 10:30.216
It's a portal, an opening through which

10:30.300 --> 10:33.302
all light, goodness, rejuvenation,
joy and ecstasy

10:33.385 --> 10:35.388
may enter the human form.

10:36.763 --> 10:37.889
- A vagina?
- Get out.

10:43.102 --> 10:45.857
<i>Hey, Stewie, 3:00. Time for The View.</i>

10:45.940 --> 10:47.191
No! No, no! Not again!

10:57.367 --> 11:00.371
Let me out of here!
I can't watch another second!

11:02.581 --> 11:06.711
Relax, Stewie. The doctor gave me this
so you can get some exercise.

11:06.794 --> 11:10.964
Boy, Stewie's more wound up than
Dad was that time he took steroids.

11:11.256 --> 11:13.842
Peter, could you please pass the potatoes?

11:14.593 --> 11:16.053
Damn it, Meg!

11:18.472 --> 11:21.766
<i>Now, back to Happy Days.
- Ah, that Fonzie is magic.</i>

11:21.892 --> 11:24.101
I love the way he hits the jukebox
to make it work.

11:24.228 --> 11:25.395
<i>What is it, Mr. C?</i>

11:25.478 --> 11:30.233
<i>Fonz, I wanted to pleasure Marion
for our anniversary, but, as you know,</i>

11:30.316 --> 11:32.403
<i>I have erectile dysfunction.</i>

11:33.737 --> 11:36.614
<i>- Oh, there we go.
- Thank you, Arthur.</i>

11:36.698 --> 11:37.657
<i>Eh.</i>

11:38.992 --> 11:42.579
Brian, will you carry me upstairs?
I want to look at my toys.

11:42.663 --> 11:45.624
- No. I'm watching television.
- Come on, I'm sick.

11:45.708 --> 11:47.459
All right. Come here.

11:53.966 --> 11:57.594
Oh, Todd, I feel like we'll never have
a baby of our own!

11:57.677 --> 12:00.347
We will, Kelly.
You just have to visualize it.

12:00.471 --> 12:04.601
Come on, close your eyes.
Picture a happy, healthy baby boy at play.

12:04.767 --> 12:08.564
Now put him in a magic bubble
and release him to the universe.

12:10.315 --> 12:13.360
Honey, now I want you to visualize
Lindsay Lohan,

12:13.484 --> 12:16.196
only, naked
and doing a backwards crab-walk.

12:16.321 --> 12:17.655
- What?
- Just do this for me!

12:19.825 --> 12:21.994
Ah, Peter! Where have you been, lad?

12:22.119 --> 12:25.623
Well, Dad, I was trying to find
my own religion, but it didn't work out.

12:25.706 --> 12:28.376
I haven't been this disappointed
since I lost my virginity.

12:32.587 --> 12:33.588
Uh-oh.

12:33.671 --> 12:35.382
You want to get some breakfast
or something?

12:35.840 --> 12:39.886
You want to find religion,
all you got to do is look in your heart.

12:40.012 --> 12:43.473
Who's always been there for you,
offering wisdom and truth?

12:43.598 --> 12:46.726
You've known him all along, Son.
Now worship him!

12:47.019 --> 12:48.979
Oh, my God! Dad's right!

12:49.062 --> 12:53.483
There is only one person and it's time
for him to be properly worshipped.

12:53.776 --> 12:56.277
I, Peter Griffin, hereby establish

12:56.361 --> 12:59.072
the First United Church of the Fonz.

12:59.363 --> 13:02.410
Fonzie, if this be your will, give me a sign.

13:05.871 --> 13:09.124
Hi, I'm Lindsay Lohan.
This is how a crab walks.

13:09.208 --> 13:11.710
It sure is! Fonzie be praised!

13:17.048 --> 13:20.511
All right, Dad.
Two days ago, this was an old barn.

13:20.635 --> 13:24.055
And now, thanks to you,
it's an old barn with a sign on it.

13:24.180 --> 13:27.892
All things are possible through
the Lord God, Arthur Fonzarelli, Son.

13:28.059 --> 13:30.603
- So, you're really going through with this?
- Absolutely.

13:30.728 --> 13:32.897
You know this place only cost me $100?

13:33.022 --> 13:35.774
That's a better deal than that
Aaron Neville megaphone I bought.

13:35.900 --> 13:39.821
Okay, I wanna thank you guys for
making me Activity Director for the day.

13:39.946 --> 13:41.907
Okay, first of all, can...

13:44.075 --> 13:46.661
What the hell?
What the hell's wrong with this thing?

13:46.744 --> 13:49.122
Okay, we're about to start the...

13:53.960 --> 13:57.338
Peter, it's not a good idea
to be putting these flyers all over town.

13:57.422 --> 13:59.048
People are gonna think you're crazy.

13:59.132 --> 14:01.092
Hey, how'd you like to lose
a bunch of teeth?

14:01.176 --> 14:03.970
I'm sorry, Lois, that was way more than
