15:46.155 --> 15:49.032
"though I suffereth
from temporary blindness.

15:49.158 --> 15:53.538
"And yea, for I am holy,
befriendeth I will Sticks Downey,

15:53.829 --> 15:56.331
"the only negro in the state of Wisconsin. "
Amen.

15:56.456 --> 15:57.459
Amen.

16:02.379 --> 16:04.548
- Brian, what's that smell?
- Black spray paint.

16:04.840 --> 16:08.761
- What were you painting?
Oh, you think you're so funny.

16:08.927 --> 16:12.014
Well, as soon as I figure out where I am,
you're dead, Brian!

16:13.224 --> 16:15.851
Damn it, I haven't been this dizzy
since I did those helium whippets

16:15.935 --> 16:17.311
at that birthday party.

16:17.645 --> 16:19.772
Okay, okay, ready? Here goes.

16:20.189 --> 16:22.525
I'm a female. I have a high voice.

16:22.608 --> 16:24.860
I have reproductive organs inside of me.

16:25.027 --> 16:26.319
And I buy groceries.

16:26.696 --> 16:29.657
Peter, your religion is an abomination.

16:29.865 --> 16:32.826
I never thought you could ever
embarrass me more in a church

16:32.909 --> 16:34.703
than you did
at your cousin Mary's wedding.

16:34.912 --> 16:38.416
And if anyone knows of any reason
why these two should not be married,

16:38.541 --> 16:40.167
let him speak now.

16:41.585 --> 16:42.753
Really?

16:43.170 --> 16:45.089
Nobody's gonna speak up.

16:45.214 --> 16:47.883
I'm the one who's gonna have to say it.

16:48.258 --> 16:49.552
All right.

16:49.759 --> 16:51.512
Genital warts.

16:51.930 --> 16:54.307
But, Dad, you're the one who said
I should look into my heart

16:54.432 --> 16:57.184
- to find my religion.
- Yes. Real religion.

16:57.267 --> 16:59.186
What I saw today wasn't religion.

16:59.270 --> 17:03.565
It was just a bunch of sheep, singing songs
and listening to ridiculous tall tales.

17:03.691 --> 17:06.110
- Actually, that is religion.
- Shut your trap, Brian.

17:06.192 --> 17:08.611
Hah! You tell him.
- Why? I agree with you.

17:08.737 --> 17:11.407
All Peter's done is found another way
to exploit people's ignorance,

17:11.531 --> 17:12.742
and that's just wrong.

17:12.866 --> 17:14.993
You think I'm...

17:16.704 --> 17:19.081
See, Brian,
that's a word the Fonz can't say,

17:19.164 --> 17:21.959
because all is right
when you welcome Fonzie into your life.

17:22.084 --> 17:23.377
Fonzie be with you.

17:23.461 --> 17:26.463
I ought to take off my belt
and slap the crap out of him.

17:26.547 --> 17:29.257
Look, Francis.
I don't like you and you don't like me.

17:29.341 --> 17:32.177
But I suggest we set aside our differences
and work together.

17:32.303 --> 17:34.095
I have an idea
of how to snap Peter out of this.

17:34.221 --> 17:36.682
Work together? You and me?

17:36.807 --> 17:38.891
Sure, sometimes opposites
work well together.

17:38.975 --> 17:40.144
In fact, Peter taught me that.

17:59.370 --> 18:01.040
Reverend Peter, I gotta talk to you.

18:01.164 --> 18:03.792
Last night I had sex with a teenage blonde
and her mother.

18:03.916 --> 18:07.462
Well, that's quite a story, Quagmire,
but my church doesn't have confession.

18:07.545 --> 18:09.298
So there's really no reason
for you to tell me.

18:09.381 --> 18:12.176
Are you kidding? I'm telling everybody.
Giggity Goo Ga!

18:14.678 --> 18:17.430
Let us pause to reflect
on the sacred mystery

18:17.513 --> 18:19.723
of Richie's elder brother, Chuck,

18:19.849 --> 18:23.395
who ascended the stairs
with his basketball in Season One

18:23.519 --> 18:25.272
and never came down again.

18:25.356 --> 18:27.023
There's just one problem, Peter.

18:27.149 --> 18:30.152
When a religion gets too powerful,
it's bound to have imitators.

18:30.236 --> 18:31.612
What are you talking about?

18:31.696 --> 18:34.156
Hi. I'm Sherman Hemsley
and I've just established

18:34.239 --> 18:35.866
the Church of George Jefferson.

18:35.991 --> 18:37.910
Who wants to move on up?

18:40.995 --> 18:42.163
Hi, I'm Gavin MacLeod

18:42.289 --> 18:44.624
and I've just established
the Church of Captain Stubing.

18:44.708 --> 18:45.917
Who wants to come onboard?

18:49.045 --> 18:50.505
Hi, I'm Kirk Cameron.

18:50.589 --> 18:53.550
Oh, great. You here to convert people
to the Church of Mike Seaver?

18:53.633 --> 18:56.511
No, I'm here to convert people
to Christianity.

18:56.594 --> 18:57.637
Okay.

18:58.096 --> 19:00.265
<i>Well, he was on Growing Pains.</i>

19:00.390 --> 19:02.516
I can't believe it. Everybody's gone.

19:02.600 --> 19:05.061
Well, people like that
are always looking for the next voice

19:05.144 --> 19:06.270
to tell them what to do.

19:06.396 --> 19:09.024
And here I was,
thinking I was making a difference.

19:09.107 --> 19:11.359
I thought I was actually connecting
with people.

19:11.443 --> 19:14.112
Could there be anyone stupider than me?

19:15.364 --> 19:17.907
- Madonna?
- Oh, yeah. She's pretty stupid.

19:18.032 --> 19:20.035
That's something we can all agree on,
right?

19:20.202 --> 19:23.370
- Absolutely, yeah. Francis?
- Oh, major idiot. Major idiot.

19:23.496 --> 19:24.705
Yeah, yeah. Well, gosh!

19:24.789 --> 19:27.083
I guess we do have some common ground
here after all, huh?

19:27.208 --> 19:30.879
Yeah. And La Isla Bonita, not a real place.
I looked it up. Couldn't find it.

19:30.963 --> 19:33.799
- Bought a globe. Couldn't find it.
- Oh, yeah? That makes her a liar, too.

19:33.923 --> 19:35.717
- She's awful.
- Awful, awful woman.

19:35.801 --> 19:37.552
- I agree, yeah.
- And she's a whore.

19:37.635 --> 19:40.430
- Oh yeah, big time.
- Oh, everybody. Canseco?

19:40.972 --> 19:43.141
- Dennis Rodman.
- Dennis Rodman, right. Right, yeah.

19:43.266 --> 19:44.560
Rodman? My God!

19:44.642 --> 19:46.184
I think he lost all his money, didn't he?

19:46.269 --> 19:48.897
Rodman lost? You sure
you're not thinking of MC Hammer?

19:49.021 --> 19:52.566
No, no, I think... Well, him, too.
I read somewhere, I think it was in like,

19:52.734 --> 19:53.943
<i>like Stuff, or is it...</i>

19:54.068 --> 19:57.530
<i>No, no, no. You know what,
it was on Real Sports with Bryant Gumbel.</i>

19:57.656 --> 20:00.117
And they said that
he's in the poorhouse now, yeah.

20:00.200 --> 20:01.242
You think she'd do him now?

20:01.367 --> 20:03.953
What, would Madonna do Rodman now?

20:04.079 --> 20:05.830
Oh, yeah, no,
'cause it's not about the money.

20:05.955 --> 20:07.039
It's about pissing off Daddy.

20:07.123 --> 20:08.750
That's right. She's got a lot of problems.

20:08.833 --> 20:10.584
- Lot of problems.
- Yeah, we are smarter.

20:10.710 --> 20:14.756
- We are smarter than Madonna.
- Oh, no question.

20:15.966 --> 20:18.093
Well, I should probably get out
of these robes.

20:22.806 --> 20:26.726
- Oh, look at you. You're all better.
- That's right, Brian. And you are toast.

20:26.809 --> 20:28.977
I'm gonna get in the gym, get my lats back

20:29.103 --> 20:32.773
and then me and my friends from
Cobra Kai are gonna take you down, man.

20:32.857 --> 20:35.817
Listen, sorry I had to rain on your parade,
Peter.

20:35.943 --> 20:37.361
It's all right, Brian.

20:37.487 --> 20:40.406
I guess the Church of the Fonz
was just a bad idea.

20:40.490 --> 20:44.993
Not really, Peter. You were preaching
honesty, friendship, courage.

20:45.286 --> 20:49.290
And if you manage to inspire
even one person to embrace those values

20:49.372 --> 20:50.916
then you are a success.

20:51.000 --> 20:53.752
Thanks, Lois.
But I doubt there's any chance of that.

20:53.753 --> 21:54.753
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru